 "_comment": [
  "Measured per-trial model spend. Every row is one real Harbor trial that reached a verdict or a",
  "kill, read from its own result.json in the source repository; nothing here is estimated.",
  "",
  "This file exists because the budget model priced a trial at a $3.50 literal sitting under a",
  "heading that said 'measured', and three phases produced no measured cost at all. The mean here",
  "is $9.95 and the median $7.74, so the figure the plan was built on was low by roughly 2.8x.",
  "",
  "Rows with reward null are runs the harness killed before a verdict. Their SPEND IS REAL and they",
  "are kept in the cost denominator on purpose: a plan that only prices the runs that finished is",
  "the same optimistic error as one that only prices the families that shipped.",
  "",
  "Rows under $0.50 are cheat/no-op probes that terminated in seconds. They are preserved but",
  "excluded from the summary statistics, which is stated wherever those statistics are used."
